# The LIGHT gate: eslint + prettier on the STAGED files only (lint-staged), then `complete:light:gates`.
# Staged-only so a peer session's dirty file cannot fail an unrelated commit; CI lints the whole tree.
# It keeps every static check (type-check, lint, both spec lints, format, the contract-bundle, docs and
# cross-repo checks) plus the unit and cross-cutting suites — nothing that starts `mongod`.
#
# Left out, apart from the staged files `test:staged` runs at the end, so run the full
# `npm run complete` by hand before merging a lane and once on main after
# each merge (CI still runs all of it):
#
# - `test:integration`, `test:contract` and `test:fuzz` — the database and HTTP layers, fuzz being
#   most of the full gate's minutes;
# - `docs:build`.
#
# The spec-identity check SKIPS rather than fails when the paired frontend is not on disk, so a
# half-cloned pair can still commit. It stays fatal under CI, where a missing sibling means the
# workflow is misconfigured.
#
# Deliberately not here, and run by hand for the occasions that want them: `test:mutation`
# (re-executes the unit suite once per mutant — nightly in CI), `complete:manual` (`test:prism`,
# which binds a real port), and `bench` (needs a running server, and reports numbers
# rather than a verdict).
# Write the generated artefacts first, so the gates below read them off disk, then check that what
# is being COMMITTED is current. The hook never stages anything: a regenerated file you did not
# stage is not in the commit, and the check below refuses the commit for it instead of papering
# over it. Costs about thirty seconds for each half.
#
# `--no-sync` is not optional. A full `regenerate` ends with `sync:frontend`, which writes into the
# PAIRED REPO's working tree — a commit here would silently dirty a checkout you are not looking
# at, and possibly one with its own work in progress. Hand the files over deliberately, with
# `npm run regenerate` by itself, when you mean to.
#
# What stays committed and is therefore checked: `shared/rules/schemas/*.json`,
# `shared/authorization-keys.generated.yaml`, `docker/crontab`, `docker/Dockerfile.dockerignore` and the
# tables inside `docs/`. Everything else `regenerate` writes (`openapi.yaml`, both asyncapi
# bundles, `api/`, every `*.generated.ts`) is gitignored: postinstall rebuilds it, and the gates
# below read it off disk.
#
# `check:generated` exports the index (`git checkout-index`, so a partial `git commit -- <paths>`
# is honoured) to a scratch folder, regenerates there and fails if anything changed. It names the
# files; the fix is `npm run regenerate` and staging them.
npm run regenerate -- --no-sync
npm run check:generated

npx lint-staged
npm run complete:light:gates

# Last, because it is the one step that starts `mongod`: every integration, contract or fuzz test
# file this commit adds or changes, run by file. Light skips those layers, so a new one would
# otherwise first run at merge time. See scripts/testing/run-staged-tests.ts.
npm run test:staged
